  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">VACR-Enhance access to Justice</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ultimately, the project aims to raise awareness and understanding, provide legal aid and representative defense at court for community, contribute suggestions to draft legal documents related to disadvantaged and vulnerable groups, especially women and children in accordance with the Constitution (2013) and relevant legal documents. Accordingly, project activities embrace these following specific goals: Outcome 1: Raising public&#x2019;s awareness and understanding about the law on administrative sanctions and criminal handling against girls and students in primary, middle and high school in Hanoi. Specifically, 28,800 children and their families were provided with information directly and indirectly through programs and activities to propagate legal education.On the same note, it is expected to attract 10,000 visits on social platforms (facebook, youtube, official press channels,..)Outcome 2: Raising public&#x2019;s awareness about the law on punishment and criminal handling for child sexual abuse, skills to preventsexual abuse against girls amongst mothers and grandmothers. Specifically, 500 mothers and grandmothers are provided with legal education. All of them access informationthrough online platforms (facebook, youtube, web and press channels).Outcome 3: Raising awareness of the community, including teachers, people working in school, educational institutions about abuse prevention skills. Accordingly, the expected number of teachers with access to training is 540.Outcome 4: Appointing lawyers from Lawyers Association for Protection of Children&apos;s Rights to participate in protecting children who are survivors of sexual abuse. Appointing lawyers to provide children and families with legal advicerelated to children&apos;s rights. This aims to have 20 cases received legal advice, 10 cases supported at the court to protect the legitimate rights and interests of children in criminal cases.Output 5: Contributing comments to 02 draft legal documents related to children&#x2019;s rights.</narrative>
  </description>
